      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to want to stop pretending when the cost of continuing feels too high, and acknowledging a part of yourself as damaged is often a necessary first step toward peace. However, acknowledging a flaw isn't the same as deciding to remain stuck; there is a vast difference between accepting pain and finally giving up on living through it. Would you be willing to consider just pausing to rest for a little while, even if the idea of \"fixing\" yourself feels entirely useless right now, so you can breathe without that expectation?",
